WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
This is the setup for SFX for Legal. You will open a matter,
file a document, have someone at the firm approve it, and
then ask the client to type their name. The pictures use an

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:50.000
From the front page, choose Open a matter. This screen is
Get Started. Type the firm name, your email, and a password
of at least 12 characters. Type the password again. Check

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:20.000
If a check fails, the firm is not created. This picture
shows three messages at once. The password must be at least
12 characters. The two passwords must match. You must agree

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:50.000
The next time, choose Sign in. Use the same email and
password, then choose Sign In. Remember me keeps you signed
in on this browser. Forgot password does not send an email.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:15.000
After sign-in you land on the dashboard. It counts open
matters, documents waiting for approval, and documents filed
this month. The counts in this picture belong to the example

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:35.000
In the left column, choose Matters. These are the cases, and
the documents that belong to them. A new firm has an empty
list and a button labeled Open matter. This example already

00:02:35.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Choose Open matter. Two boxes appear: Matter, and Client.
Both are required. The example uses Hartwell acquisition and
Hartwell Holdings. Use the real matter and the real client.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Open the matter. Under Add a document, choose the file, then
choose File on this matter. That button stays gray until a
file is chosen. The screen refuses a file larger than 6 MB.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:55.000
On that document row, choose Request approval. That adds a
waiting decision on Approvals. It does not email anyone, and
it does not send the file to the client. Request approval

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Choose Approvals. A waiting document is marked pending, and
it has Approve and Reject. Approve means someone at the firm
has released it. Reject leaves it on the matter. It does not

00:04:30.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Go back to the matter. The lower card asks someone to accept
a document. This records a typed name. It does not send the
document to DocuSign. Choose the document. Type the signer

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:35.000
The client does not need an account. The page is titled
Accept this document. It names your firm, the file, the
matter, and the client. They type their name and choose

00:05:35.000 --> 00:06:00.000
After a real submission, the page says, Your acceptance is
recorded. There is no separate signed PDF on this screen.
The record is the typed name, the time, and the document

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Choose Signature requests. A finished request is marked
signed. The row names the document, the signer, the email
you entered, the matter, the time, and the name they typed.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Choose Team and client access. The person who created the
firm is the Owner, and cannot be removed on this page. An
Admin can manage people and settings. A Member can work with

00:06:50.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Choose Invite Member. Type their email. Choose Member or
Admin. Then choose Send Invite. Member is for someone who
should work on files. Admin is for someone who should manage

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:45.000
The green notice says no email is sent. Share the link
yourself. Choose Copy link and paste it into your own
message. Until that person opens the link and creates a

00:07:45.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Their link opens Accept invitation. It names the firm and
the email you invited. They type their name, a password of
at least 12 characters, and the same password again. Then

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:35.000
Choose Compliance reports. The list shows who opened a
matter, filed a document, requested approval, approved or
rejected it, invited someone, and recorded an acceptance.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:09:15.000
Choose Settings, then General. The organization name is
saved, and it shows at the top of the signed-in pages. The
expiration number and the max-downloads number are saved on

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:45.000
Choose Settings, then Billing, only when you mean to look at
the plan. A new firm is on Trial. No card is on file. The
date on this card is the example firm's date, not yours.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:10:10.000
You are done when you can sign in, a matter has both names,
a document is filed, Approvals shows it as approved, you
sent the acceptance link yourself, the client sees the words

